{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":773,"code_snippet":"cp \"$WS/.eval/model-invoke.jsonl\" \"$EVALD/model-invoke.jsonl\" 2>/dev/null || true","finding":"Host-side driver dereferences sandbox-controlled symlinks when copying ledgers and dissent envelopes out of the sandbox; a planted link exfiltrates any operator-readable host file into persisted eval artefacts.","reasoning_trace":"Traced sandbox-writable .eval/ (info/exclude only, :476) to host-side cp/wc/sed at :713,:715,:769,:773,:774,:777; container runs as host uid on a bind mount (:686) so link targets resolve on the host; verified cp 9.1 dereferences a symlink source operand.","critique":"The sandbox is UNTRUSTED per the harness's own trust model (sandbox-mount.sh:97-99, DEC-0413) but its filesystem metadata is trusted.","remediation":"Refuse symlinks and non-regular files before every host-side read of a sandbox path; copy with cp -P after the check; add a bats case planting a symlink that expects infrastructure_error.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/59.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/lib/sandbox-mount.sh","line":513,"code_snippet":"PROJECT_ROOT=\"$ws\" bash \"$ubs\" --opt-out \"eval sandbox: br not on PATH\"","finding":"init_sandbox_beads executes the sandbox's .claude/scripts/beads/update-beads-state.sh on the host, outside the container, whenever br is absent; :386 has the same shape for the prompt tree's tools/gen-checksums.sh.","reasoning_trace":"pipeline-run.sh:489 calls init_sandbox_beads on the host before any container starts; the script path is under $ws/.claude, copied from --source-tree (:131); header :97-99 states no harness script may source .claude/ code; pipeline-run.bats:248-259 scans source lines only.","critique":"Defeats the container, two-mount rule, read-only root and env allowlist for a PR-controlled script.","remediation":"Write the opt-out marker from the library; always use the inline hashing path for the sandbox manifest; extend the trust-boundary test to exec of $ws/.claude or $EVAL_PROMPT_TREE paths.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/829.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/668.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/preflight.sh","line":190,"code_snippet":"ACTUAL_COUNT=$(git -C \"${MANIFEST_TREE}\" ls-files -- .claude | awk ... | wc -l)","finding":"git ls-files reads the index, so a tracked .claude/ fence file deleted from the working tree is still counted and the count mismatch the previous find-based check detected is suppressed.","reasoning_trace":"Diff base→head replaces find -type f with git ls-files; the find fallback at :196 runs only when the tracked count is 0; confirms review Changes Required #5 and the review dissent's BLOCKING finding.","critique":"Preflight runs before every skill and is the strict-mode exit-1 gate (:204-214).","remediation":"Count only tracked paths that exist in the working tree, or subtract git ls-files --deleted; add a deleted-file unit case.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/354.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/check-loa.sh","line":75,"code_snippet":"elif [[ \"$submodule_mount\" == \"true\" && -f \".loa/${file}\" ]]; then not_mounted=$((not_mounted + 1))","finding":"On a submodule mount every absent manifest path exists under .loa/ by construction, so the Missing branch is unreachable: a deleted fence link is informational not-mounted and the exit code stays 0.","reasoning_trace":"submodule_mount set from -d .loa/.claude (:64); base reported Missing + exit 1; no hash comparison of .loa/<path>; no deleted-link bats case; raised by both dissents (review advisory, audit DISS-C-001).","critique":"Together with SEC-003 both downstream integrity checks pass after a fence is deleted.","remediation":"Use the mount's link inventory to distinguish never-linked from removed; treat a path as Missing when its parent dir is linked; compare .loa/<path> hash in the not-mounted branch; add the deleted-link case.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/354.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":770,"code_snippet":"(.cost_micro_usd // ((.cost_usd // 0) * 1000000))] | add // 0 | round","finding":"Sandbox-written cost-ledger rows are summed without a sign or type clamp; a negative row makes SPENT_MICRO negative, inflates the watchdog budget and defeats the per-run cap. Same in ablation-row.sh:242,312 and spend.sh:129.","reasoning_trace":"Followed ledger_micro into SPENT_MICRO (:854), budget (:719) and the cap check (:864); the ledger lives in agent-writable sandbox/.eval/.","critique":"The thing being metered controls part of the meter.","remediation":"select numeric and >= 0 per row; clamp to [0, cap]; same in spend.sh and ablation-row.sh.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":686,"code_snippet":"\"$DOCKER_BIN\" run --rm --name \"$cname\" --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" --network bridge --read-only --tmpfs /tmp:rw,size=1g --pids-limit 512 --memory 4g --cpus 2","finding":"Container for an autonomous bypass-permissions agent lacks --cap-drop=ALL and --security-opt=no-new-privileges; Debian slim ships setuid su/mount/passwd/chsh etc.; egress unrestricted.","reasoning_trace":"Read the docker argv assembly :685-696 and the resource-flag test :632-657; checked the setuid set of a Debian base.","critique":"Read-only root and non-root uid limit but do not remove local escalation surface.","remediation":"Add --cap-drop=ALL --security-opt=no-new-privileges:true; consider an egress-restricted network; assert in the bats resource-flags case.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-007","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":570,"code_snippet":"if [[ -f \"$CREDS_HOME/.codex/$f\" ]]; then cp \"$CREDS_HOME/.codex/$f\" \"$HOME_DIR/.codex/$f\"; fi","finding":"Operator Codex auth.json is copied under <run>/meta/home, mounted rw into the agent's container, and survives a SIGKILLed driver inside a results tree that batch tooling archives.","reasoning_trace":"make_home :563-573; cleanup only in finish/on_exit (:348,:356); header :104-106 acknowledges SIGKILL leaves records behind.","critique":"A run tree is not a credential store; the agent under test receives a long-lived operator OAuth token.","remediation":"Place the per-run HOME outside the run tree (mktemp -d) or mount the codex files read-only from a dedicated 0700 dir; sweep stale homes; use a scoped eval credential.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/459.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-008","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":725,"code_snippet":"exec \"${full[@]}\" ) < /dev/null > \"$events\" 2> \"$errf\" &","finding":"Transcripts and stderr are persisted raw with no redaction of SECRET_KEYS values the driver knows; the only guard (pipeline-run.bats:726) is a bare negated grep inside a for loop that cannot fail.","reasoning_trace":"Agent env carries AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK; any env dump lands in events-<label>.jsonl which ablation-row.sh and batch artefacts keep; bash exempts ! from errexit (review #4).","critique":"The advertised guarantee 'no secret in any capture or log' is neither enforced nor tested.","remediation":"Post-phase scan of events/stderr for every set secret value → redact or infrastructure_error; make the bats assertions failing with run ! grep.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/532.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-009","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/took-effect.sh","line":266,"code_snippet":"[[ \"$filesha\" == \"$msha\" ]] && EVID=\"$EVID (matches checksums.json)\"","finding":"integrity_clean never enforces the driver-recorded manifest_sha256; tamper-then-regenerate passes, and the walk iterates manifest entries only so injected .claude/ files are invisible.","reasoning_trace":"Read rule_integrity_clean :234-268; msha fetched but only compared for decoration; confirms review Observation §1.","critique":"The one driver-owned anchor is ignored.","remediation":"FAIL on filesha != msha; FAIL on unlisted regular files under sandbox/.claude/.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/354.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-010","category":"devops","criterion":"ci_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.github/workflows/bats-tests.yml","line":178,"code_snippet":"bash tools/gen-checksums.sh --check","finding":"The new integrity-manifest gate is red on this PR: ten manifest-covered files change and no .claude/checksums.json is regenerated; the paths: filter also omits .claude/skills, protocols, rules, loa and the manifest itself.","reasoning_trace":"gen-checksums.sh:143-168 exits 1 on absent/drifted manifest; head.diff carries no checksums.json; review observed DRIFT 10 paths.","critique":"An integrity gate that cannot pass is bypassed in practice.","remediation":"Run tools/gen-checksums.sh and commit the manifest; extend the paths filter.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/354.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-011","category":"security","criterion":"supply_chain","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/Dockerfile.ablation","line":91,"code_snippet":"ENV NPM_CONFIG_IGNORE_SCRIPTS=true","finding":"ignore-scripts is set where the agent never reads it (exec shim allowlist drops the env; :77 writes /root/.npmrc while the process runs as host uid with HOME=/home/evaluser), so npm lifecycle scripts of anything the agent installs run.","reasoning_trace":"Cross-checked PASS_KEYS/envkv at pipeline-run.sh:631,661-670 and make_home :563-573.","critique":"The comment at :76 is false.","remediation":"Add NPM_CONFIG_IGNORE_SCRIPTS to the pass-through keys or write ignore-scripts=true into $HOME_DIR/.npmrc in make_home.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/829.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-012","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/preflight.sh","line":184,"code_snippet":"MANIFEST_LINK=$(readlink \"${PROJECT_ROOT}/.claude/checksums.json\")","finding":"The checksums.json symlink target is unconstrained; git runs in whatever tree the link names and honours that repo's config (fsmonitor/hooksPath).","reasoning_trace":"Dissent DISS-C-002; verified the derivation :183-187.","remediation":"Require MANIFEST_TREE to be PROJECT_ROOT or PROJECT_ROOT/.loa; pass -c core.fsmonitor=false -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/59.html"]}
